    <exercise number="5" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>If you perform your break-even analysis and there is more than one solution, explain how you would determine which x-values are profit and which are not.</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>Choose any number between each solution and plug into $$C(x) C(x)$$ and $$R(x). R(x).$$ If $$C(x)&lt;R(x), C(x)&lt;R(x),$$ then there is profit.</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
